<title>USA: Lockheed McDonnell win missile work.</title>
<headline>Lockheed McDonnell win missile work.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDonnell Douglas Corp and Lockheed Martin units on Friday were named as finalists for the U.S. Air Force's $2 billion program to build a new space missile to replace the one currently deployed.</p>
<p>McDonnell Douglas Aerospace of Huntington Beach, Calif. and Lockheed Martin Corp.'s Astronautics Division near Denver were awarded $60 million contracts each and will compete for the final contract in mid-1988 to build the new missiles. The other bidders were Alliant Techsystems and Boeing Defense and Space Group but Boeing plans to merge with McDonnell Douglas.</p>
</text>
